n": "Is the U.S. college system a great equalizer or a cause of growing inequality? Improved access to higher education has brought millions of Americans into the middle class, and yet rising selectivity has meant that a disproportionate share of the economic elite come from a few top colleges. This course will explore the three big parts of the college experience --- (1) admissions and the college-going decision; (2) education while in college; and (3) college completion and labor market entry --- and ask how each part contributes to inequality in economic outcomes. Lectures and readings will focus on simple economic theories of higher education as well as the empirical methods used to test these theories.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "Enrollment preference given to: \nILRLE 3445: ILR juniors and seniors.\nECON 3770: undergraduate sophomores, juniors, and seniors.", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "ILRLE 2400 or ECON 3030.", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "IL", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2026SP, 2025SP, 2024SP, 2023SP", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2923, "crseId": 371462, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "ILRLE", "catalogNbr": "3460", "titleShort": "Econ of Lbr Mrkt in 21st Cent", "titleLong": "Economics of the Labor Market in the 21st Century", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-AG", "descr": "AG-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distributio